--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: EVALUATION_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 88394cb8bd95fea42af63c537ab05d35, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 808531789459456
    m_Localized: Correct!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 808531818819584
    m_Localized: Incorrect!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 808531818819585
    m_Localized: Write your answer...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 810621471404032
    m_Localized: Your answer was correct!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 810621475598336
    m_Localized: 'The correct answer(s):'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285730893824
    m_Localized: True
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285827362816
    m_Localized: False
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285827362817
    m_Localized: News headlines always accurately reflect the content of the article
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285827362818
    m_Localized: By reading only the headline I can tell whether a piece of news
      is false or not
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285827362819
    m_Localized: We should always read the entire article to evaluate its truthfulness
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285827362820
    m_Localized: "If the news comes from someone close to me, I don\u2019t need to
      verify it"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285827362821
    m_Localized: A strong, striking headline means the news is true
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285831557120
    m_Localized: By reading the whole article, I can pay attention to the language
      to assess its truthfulness
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285831557121
    m_Localized: Headlines are not disinformation, since their purpose is to inform
      the reader
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285831557122
    m_Localized: All the news we find on the internet is false, and we can only trust
      print press or television
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285831557123
    m_Localized: A headline is a good summary of a news story
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285831557124
    m_Localized: The date in a news story is an important indicator for assessing
      its reliability
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285831557125
    m_Localized: "A news story that uses subjective judgments such as insults or
      strongly reflects the author\u2019s opinion may be less reliable"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285831557126
    m_Localized: All news published on the internet is reliable because everything
      is checked before it is posted
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285831557127
    m_Localized: If my family or friends send me some news, there is no need to check
      the source
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285831557128
    m_Localized: If a friend or relative sends me news without a reliable source,
      I should be suspicious and verify it using official sources
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751424
    m_Localized: "I don\u2019t need to check the source of information I receive
      via WhatsApp or text message; these channels are always reliable"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751425
    m_Localized: Which of the following is a reliable source of information on financial
      matters?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751426
    m_Localized: My bank
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751427
    m_Localized: Internet
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751428
    m_Localized: Family members and/or friends
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751429
    m_Localized: What should I do before sharing a news story?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751430
    m_Localized: Check the source
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751431
    m_Localized: See how many times it has been shared
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751432
    m_Localized: Make sure it contains images
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751433
    m_Localized: "All information sources are equally untrustworthy; you can\u2019t
      trust any of them"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751434
    m_Localized: "A journalist\u2019s age is an important factor when evaluating
      a news story. "
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751435
    m_Localized: 'The gender of a journalist is an important factor to consider when
      evaluating a news story. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751436
    m_Localized: 'If a close contact sends me a news story, I can trust that it is
      true. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751437
    m_Localized: 'Which of the following sources are most reliable on health issues:'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751438
    m_Localized: Public Health Department
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751439
    m_Localized: An online blog
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751440
    m_Localized: A comment under a news article
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751441
    m_Localized: A news story in a well-known newspaper
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751442
    m_Localized: A video on a social network
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751443
    m_Localized: "If a piece of information fits my prior beliefs, I don\u2019t need
      to double-check it.  "
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751444
    m_Localized: "If information causes strong emotions (fear, anger\u2026), that
      means it is reliable.  "
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751445
    m_Localized: If a news story shows official statistics and cites its sources,
      the information is reliable.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751446
    m_Localized: If I know that the information comes from a reliable source...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751447
    m_Localized: 'If many people have shared something online, that is a good sign
      it is true.  '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751448
    m_Localized: "When I have doubts about whether a news story is true, I should\u2026"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751449
    m_Localized: Why do fake news stories try to make us angry?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751450
    m_Localized: Because the people behind them are evil and their only goal is to
      make us hate others.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285835751451
    m_Localized: Because when we are angry, we are less likely to think critically
      about the information.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140032
    m_Localized: 'All news, both real and fake, is trying to make us angry. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140033
    m_Localized: 'If I receive information by SMS, there is no need to double-check
      it because that channel is always reliable.  '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140034
    m_Localized: 'If a news story shows that I am right about something, that news
      must be correct.  '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140035
    m_Localized: 'Loyalty to a media outlet (such as a newspaper) is more important
      than checking information with other sources.  '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140036
    m_Localized: 'When we are unsure whether a news story is real or not, we should:'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140037
    m_Localized: Ask an AI such as ChatGPT whether it is true
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140038
    m_Localized: Check how many times it has been shared
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140039
    m_Localized: Compare it with other media outlets and look for the original sources
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140040
    m_Localized: 'If a news story contains images, that means the news is reliable.  '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140041
    m_Localized: 'I can trust everything that is published on the internet because
      it is checked beforehand.  '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140042
    m_Localized: 'News that contain images are reliable because the images are reliable
      proof of the information.  '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140043
    m_Localized: "When I have doubts about the truthfulness of a news story, I should\u2026"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140044
    m_Localized: Share it with others to see what they think
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140045
    m_Localized: Avoid that information because it may be false
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140046
    m_Localized: Go to a fact-checker such as Maldita.es or an official source
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140047
    m_Localized: Every news outlet has political biases that will affect its news
      coverage and the level of detail it gives to each story.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140050
    m_Localized: 'If I find out that a close contact has sent me fake news, it is
      better to say nothing than to give my opinion about it.  '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140051
    m_Localized: 'If I hear a news story very often in the media, it must be because
      it is real.  '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140052
    m_Localized: 'As a general rule, when evaluating interviews, the following are
      more reliable:'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140053
    m_Localized: Experts/scientists on the topic
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140054
    m_Localized: Anonymous interview
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285844140055
    m_Localized: Opinion pieces
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285848334336
    m_Localized: 'When an emergency alert arrives, we should always share it immediately
      without hesitation.  '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285848334337
    m_Localized: 'It is not necessary to read news from different sources if the
      ones we use are reliable.  '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285848334338
    m_Localized: 'Some people are more likely than others to forward fake news.  '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285848334339
    m_Localized: 'It is important to review the editorial line of the media outlets
      I use to inform myself.  '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285848334340
    m_Localized: 'If I already have a trusted outlet, there is no need to read information
      from other media.  '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285848334341
    m_Localized: 'If a news story describes a situation that makes me very angry
      or upset, it is important to calm down before checking the information.  '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285848334342
    m_Localized: It is important to compare news with other sources that do not share
      the same political ideology.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285848334343
    m_Localized: To assess how credible an information source is, it is important
      to know who its main financial backers are.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285848334344
    m_Localized: 'When we see videos or images related to a news story, it is important
      to look for watermarks or other signs that they may have been generated by
      AI.  '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285848334345
    m_Localized: 'Possible reasons why someone might create a fake news story include:'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285848334346
    m_Localized: Political interests
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285848334347
    m_Localized: Economic interests
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285848334348
    m_Localized: Stirring up hatred, one of the emotions most likely to spread
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285848334349
    m_Localized: Comic or mocking intentions
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7138285848334350
    m_Localized: Because of a distorted view of reality
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213551790002176
    m_Localized: Very well! Sometimes headlines can be misleading or sensationalist
      in order to attract our attention and do not accurately reflect the content
      of the news story.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213551991328768
    m_Localized: Beware! This is false. Sometimes headlines can be misleading or
      sensationalist in order to attract our attention and do not accurately reflect
      the content of the news story.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552003911680
    m_Localized: You're right! To be sure of the accuracy of a news story, it's important
      to always read it in its entirety.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552008105984
    m_Localized: Oops! This is fake. Remember, to be sure of the accuracy of a news
      story, it is important to always read it in its entirety.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552016494592
    m_Localized: 'Correct! Reading the entire news story helps us evaluate its accuracy,
      as we can look at things like the data it provides or the language it uses. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552020688896
    m_Localized: 'Be careful, this is true! Reading the entire news story helps us
      evaluate its accuracy, as we can look at things like the data it provides or
      the language it uses. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552024883200
    m_Localized: Exactly. It is always important to verify information. Sometimes
      people can share misinformation with us without realising it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552033271808
    m_Localized: Be careful, this is false. It is always important to verify information.
      Sometimes people may share misinformation with us without realising it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552033271809
    m_Localized: You're right! Headlines can be sensationalist to attract our attention,
      and that does not indicate that the information is accurate.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552045854720
    m_Localized: You're wrong, this is false. Headlines can be sensationalist to
      attract our attention, and that does not indicate that the information is true.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552045854721
    m_Localized: 'Very well! Language can be a good indicator. Disinformation tends
      to use more emotional, alarmist or sensationalist language. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552054243328
    m_Localized: 'Be careful! This is true. Language can be a good indicator. Misinformation
      often uses more emotional, alarmist or sensationalist language. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552066826240
    m_Localized: Correct! Headlines can also be manipulated to make them seem more
      appealing and therefore be misleading.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552071020544
    m_Localized: 'This is false. Remember, headlines can also be manipulated to make
      them seem more appealing and therefore be misleading. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552075214848
    m_Localized: 'That''s right! There are also reliable sources on the internet.
      You shouldn''t distrust everything. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552079409152
    m_Localized: 'Wrong! There are also reliable sources on the internet. You shouldn''t
      distrust everything. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552083603456
    m_Localized: Very well! Sometimes headlines can be misleading or sensationalist
      in order to attract our attention and do not provide a good summary of the
      news. It is important to read the entire article.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552091992064
    m_Localized: Beware! This is false. Sometimes headlines can be misleading or
      sensationalist in order to attract our attention and do not accurately summarise
      the news story. You have to read the whole thing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552096186368
    m_Localized: 'Exactly! Publication dates can help us determine whether a news
      item is recent or whether it is information taken out of context. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552100380672
    m_Localized: 'Oops! This is fake. Publication dates can help us determine whether
      a news item is recent or whether it is information taken out of context. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552108769280
    m_Localized: That's right, this is true. Reliable news outlets usually strive
      for objectivity and neutrality.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552112963584
    m_Localized: This is false. Reliable news outlets generally strive for objectivity
      and neutrality.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552117157888
    m_Localized: 'Correct! NOT everything published on the internet is true. It is
      very important to consult reliable and official sources to verify information. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552121352192
    m_Localized: You're wrong, this is false. NOT everything published on the internet
      is true. It is very important to consult reliable and official sources to verify
      information.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552129740800
    m_Localized: Exactly. It is always important to verify information. Sometimes
      people can share misinformation with us without realising it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552133935104
    m_Localized: Be careful, this is false. It is always important to verify information.
      Sometimes people may share misinformation with us without realising it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552133935105
    m_Localized: 'Very well! When the source of the news is unknown, it is ALWAYS
      important to verify the information. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552146518016
    m_Localized: 'Be careful! This is true. When the source of the news is unknown,
      it is ALWAYS important to verify the information. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552150712320
    m_Localized: 'Exactly. Even if the information comes to us through a familiar
      channel, it is always important to verify it. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552154906624
    m_Localized: Error. Even if the information comes to us through a family channel,
      it is always important to verify the information.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552163295232
    m_Localized: 'Very well! When looking for financial information, it is always
      best to go to the most official source, the bank. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552167489536
    m_Localized: 'Be careful! Remember that when looking for financial information,
      it is always best to go to the most official source, the bank. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552171683840
    m_Localized: 'You''re absolutely right! It''s always important to check the source.
      If the source is unknown, it''s best to verify the information before sharing
      it. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552175878144
    m_Localized: 'You got it wrong! It is always important to check the source. If
      the source is unknown, it is best to verify the information before sharing
      it. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552188461056
    m_Localized: 'Very well! This is false. There are reliable sources and sources
      that are not. Always remember to check the source. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552192655360
    m_Localized: 'Be careful! This is false. There are reliable sources and sources
      that are not. Always remember to check the source. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552196849664
    m_Localized: 'Correct, this is not a good indicator of truthfulness. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552201043968
    m_Localized: 'Incorrect, this is not a good indicator of truthfulness. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552205238272
    m_Localized: 'Correct, this is not a good indicator of truthfulness. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552209432576
    m_Localized: 'Incorrect, this is not a good indicator of truthfulness. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552217821184
    m_Localized: Exactly. It is always important to verify information. Sometimes
      people can share misinformation with us without realising it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552217821185
    m_Localized: Be careful, this is false. It is always important to verify information.
      Sometimes people may share misinformation with us without realising it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552226209792
    m_Localized: You're right! Sometimes content confirms my preconceived ideas,
      but that doesn't mean it's true. It's always important to verify information.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552234598400
    m_Localized: You're wrong! Sometimes content confirms my preconceived ideas,
      but that doesn't mean it's true. It's always important to verify information.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552238792704
    m_Localized: Correct! In fact, disinformation often uses these kinds of emotions
      to draw us in.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552242987008
    m_Localized: False! In fact, misinformation often uses these kinds of emotions
      to draw us in.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552247181312
    m_Localized: Yes! When a news story includes official sources or statistics,
      it is usually a sign of accuracy.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28213552251375616
    m_Localized: Be careful! This is true. When a news story includes official sources
      or statistics, it is usually a sign of veracity.
    m_Metadata:
